shoot:description:On a recent trip to the east coast, I added 17 birds to my life list.  Most of them were backyard/easy birds, but it was still great to finally see them and get some photos as well.  Highlights include some Great Black-backed Gulls on the Atlantic coast, a Broad-winged Hawk, and a Mississippi Kite, which was a local rarity in New Hampshire.  American Redstart and Yellow-throated Vireo were among my favorite nice-looking eastern birds I saw on the trip.  Some other lifers were either juveniles or otherwise not in their colorful male plumage, including Rose-breasted Grosbeak, Yellow-bellied Sapsucker, and Baltimore Oriole, but I can look forward to photographing those someday.
