2026-07-27-080312-EM130461-sm.jpg:description:I'm about as sure as I possibly could be that this was a Downy Woodpecker, but I see there aren't any visible black spots on the outer tail feathers.  I've heard of this before, and the [birdsoftheworld.org account](https://birdsoftheworld.org/bow/species/dowwoo/cur/identification#simspecies) says "Downy Woodpecker's outer rectrices are variably but usually barred black beyond the uppertail coverts (variably but usually all white in Hairy Woodpecker)".
